  "mapping": "# Risk Radar dataset mapping (D81) for IEEE-CIS Fraud Detection (Vesta, Kaggle).\n# Written 17 Sep 2026 from the published column list, then checked against the\n# downloaded files the same day (ml/datasets/join_ieee.py): every mapped column is\n# present; train 590,540 rows over 182 days, 3.50% fraud; test 506,691 rows, 30\n# days after train ends, no labels. The customer key gives 73,407 customers, half\n# with two transactions or fewer, so behavioural history is thin.\n#\n# What this dataset is: card-not-present e-commerce, with real chargeback labels.\n# What it cannot give: account transfers, declines (only processed transactions),\n# sign-in or SIM events, credits, destinations. So the rules built for Nigerian\n# transfers mostly cannot fire, and the test is mainly of the model and the method.\n#\n# Choices to check:\n# - Time: TransactionDT is seconds from an unstated start; 2017-11-30 is the common\n#   reading. Only gaps between transactions matter to the measurements.\n# - The customer: the file has no card number. card1 (issuer and card range),\n#   addr1 (billing region), P_emaildomain and card_start_day (transaction day minus\n#   D1, added by join_ieee.py) are the usual stand-in. Without card_start_day a\n#   card range reads as one card and the burst rule fired 20 times a day, all false.\n# - Labels: Vesta marks a card's later transactions fraud after a chargeback, so\n#   incidents (fraud rows of one card within 24 hours) are the fairer unit.\n# - Native features for the ceiling arm: C1-C14 (counts) and D1-D15 (day gaps),\n#   Vesta's own engineered columns. V1-V339 are left out: their meaning is not\n#   published (D10f: a column whose making cannot be read is not an input).\ndataset: IEEE-CIS Fraud Detection (Vesta)\nreviewed: true\nfields:\n  label:\n    column: isFraud\n    positive: [1]\n  incident:\n    derive: {by: customer, gap_hours: 24}\n  timestamp:\n    column: TransactionDT\n    unit: seconds\n    origin: '2017-11-30T00:00:00+00:00'\n  amount:\n    column: TransactionAmt\n    scale: 100\n  customer:\n    columns: [card1, addr1, P_emaildomain, card_start_day]\n  card:\n    columns: [card1, card2, card3, card5, addr1, P_emaildomain, card_start_day]\n  device:\n    column: DeviceInfo\n  channel:\n    constant: WEB\n  instrument:\n    constant: CARD\n  auth_result:\n    constant: APPROVED\n  region:\n    column: addr1\n  merchant_category:\n    column: ProductCD\nnative_features:\n- C1\n- C2\n- C3\n- C4\n- C5\n- C6\n- C7\n- C8\n- C9\n- C10\n- C11\n- C12\n- C13\n- C14\n- D1\n- D2\n- D3\n- D4\n- D5\n- D6\n- D7\n- D8\n- D9\n- D10\n- D11\n- D12\n- D13\n- D14\n- D15\n- dist1\n- dist2\nignore: {}\n",
